ty of RuL1–5 was determined using the shake-flask method combined with inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry (ICP-MS) analysis. The compounds were dissolved in 4 mL of a 1:1 mixture of n-octanol and Milli-Q (MQ) water. The solution was shaken at 60 rpm at 25 °C to allow partitioning between the two phases. After 24 h, the n-octanol and water layers were separated and centrifuged at 3,000 rpm for 10 min. The supernatant from each phase was collected, and 100 μL from each was mixed with 400 μL of nitric acid. The final volume was adjusted to 10 mL with MQ water. The concentrations of RuL1– RuL5 in the aqueous phase and organic phase were then quantified using ICP-MS."}]}